Description: antinomie: stop a group that was asked to stop during any continue
 STOP while a session is RESUMING only sets s->interrupt and answers;
 do_cont() takes it up when it lets the threads go. It did so only when
 a step was still in the kernel (-EINPROGRESS), and a step past a
 breakpoint checked it on its own. For a plain continue (no thread to
 step past a breakpoint), or a step that failed and resumed the group,
 the interrupt was cleared and dropped: the host had its STOP
 acknowledged, the program ran on, and the debugger waited for a stop
 that never came (the host does not repeat STOP).
 .
 - do_cont() turns any pending interrupt into STOPPING and a stop
   request once the threads run. The paths that stop on their own (a
   finished step, a deferred event, a vfork) clear the interrupt
   before, as they did.
 .
 Found by the 0.9.0 bug hunt (KDBG-6). No contract change (revision 22).
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22

---
diff --git a/kernel/antinomie/debug.c b/kernel/antinomie/debug.c
index 288859dc6..f79b98f1d 100644
--- a/kernel/antinomie/debug.c
+++ b/kernel/antinomie/debug.c
@@ -2079,8 +2079,10 @@ run:
 	insert_breakpoints(as);
 	spin_lock_irq(&s->lock);
 	memset(&s->cur, 0, sizeof(s->cur));
-	/* A stop asked for while a step was still in the kernel is done now. */
-	stop = s->interrupt && error == -EINPROGRESS;
+	/* A stop asked for while the group was being resumed (a step still in
+	 * the kernel, or a plain continue) is done now: STOP acknowledged it.
+	 */
+	stop = s->interrupt;
 	s->interrupt = false;
 	spin_unlock_irq(&s->lock);
 	session_set_state(s, ANTC_DEBUG_RUNNING);
